==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
From a West Semitic compound the second part of which is {{m|sem-pro|*salim}}, which meant either “peace” or “{{w|Shalim}} (''the Canaanite god of twilight'')”. For more information see [[ירושלים#Etymology|ירושלים]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|egy|/ʔuʀuʃalimum/|a=Middle Egyptian|ref={{R:egy:Hoch 1994|493}}}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

