etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==
{{was fwotd|egy|2024|March|24}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|egy|ꜣby|t1=lithe spotted big cat|mḥw|t2=Lower Egypt}} in a direct genitive construction, thus ‘panther of Lower Egypt’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymon|egy|:inh|afa-pro:*leb-<id:elephant>|id=elephant}}
From {{inh|egy|afa-pro|*leb-}} (compare {{cog|tan|labata}}, {{cog|moz|ʾelbi}}).<ref name=HSED>{{R:HSED|section=1662|page=360|*leb-|url=http://starling.rinet.ru/cgi-bin/response.cgi?single=1&basename=%2fdata%2fsemham%2fafaset&text_number=2513&root=config}}</ref>

Likely related to {{m|egy|ꜣb||fingernail}} via the ‘ivory, tusk’ sense.

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˈʀuːbaw|m=ˈʀuːbaw|ml=ˈjuːbə|l=ˈjeːβ}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
From {{af|egy|ꜣbwt <t:appearance, form>|nṯr <t:god>}} in a direct genitive construction, thus ‘form of the god’. However, the full form {{m|egy|*ꜣbwt-nṯr}} is unattested, as the word-final {{m|egy||t}} had fallen silent and was often left unwritten by the time of this term’s earliest attestation.{{attention|egy|Is it in fact unattested? The ''Thesaurus Linguae Aegyptiae'' lists this word as ꜣbwt-nṯr, with reference to Meeks, Dimitri, Mythes et Légendes du Delta, MIFAO 125, Le Caire 2006. I don’t have access to this work and can’t confirm that such a writing exists; Wilson contrarily gives the word as ꜣbw-nṯr and says ‘this cloth is not attested elsewhere’.}} {{egy-ht}}

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Related to {{m|egy|ꜣb||to avoid, to cease, to separate from}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|egy|/ʔəˈβap/|a=Late Egyptian}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Etymology 1===
{{unc|egy}}. A development from {{af|egy|ꜣbw|t1=elephant|ḏw|t2=mountain}} in a direct genitive construction, thus ‘elephant of the mountain’ in reference to the local topography, has been suggested.

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ʀVˈbaːcʼVw|m=ʀVˈbaːtʼVw|ml=ʔəˈbaːtʼə|l=ʔəˈβoːtʼ|V=1}}
{{egy-IPA-E|ꜣbḏ_w}}

