etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Pronunciation===
Vycichl assumes defective writing, with an unrepresented consonant {{m|egy||j}}:
{{egy-IPA-R|o=jaʀˈlaljat|m=jaʀˈlaljaʔ|ml=ʔaˈlaʔla|l=ʔaˈlaʔlə|onote=<ref>{{R:cop:Vycichl|41}}</ref>}}
Allen instead suggests the word is properly {{m|egy||jrꜣrt}}, with the order of consonants changed for calligraphic reasons;<ref>Allen, James P. (2019) ''Egyptian Phonology'', page 81</ref> Peust gives an analogous solution, though he posits metathesis rather than calligraphic reasons.<ref>{{R:egy:Peust|235}}</ref> In this case one can reconstruct:
{{egy-IPA-R|o=jaˈlaʀlat|m=jaˈlaʀlaʔ|ml=ʔaˈlaʔla|l=ʔaˈlaʔlə}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

