etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Dual form of the perfective active participle of {{m|egy|jj|t=to come}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Interjection===
{{egy-interj|head=<hiero>ii-y:D54-w-y</hiero>}}

# [[welcome]] {{gloss|greeting upon someone’s arrival}}
#* {{Q|egy||GHtO.|line 17|quote=<hiero>N9*t:Z2-nTr-Hr:Z1-r:S:zp*Z1s*Z1s-ii-w&y-Q2:ir-zA-Z1:H_SPACE-G5-mn:ib*Z1-mAa:a:P8H-zA-Z1:H_SPACE-st-t:H8-E9:a-w-iwa:H_SPACE-Q2:ir</hiero>
|tr=psḏt ḥr ršrš '''jjwj''' zꜣ wsjr ḥr mn jb mꜣꜥ-ḫrw zꜣ ꜣst jwꜥw wsjr
|t=The Ennead was rejoicing: '''Welcome''', son of Osiris, Horus, firm of heart and true of voice, son of Isis and heir of Osiris!}}

====Usage notes====
Syntactically this word functions as an adjectival predicate. It is often followed by {{m|egy|m ḥtp||in peace}}, sometimes with an intervening pronoun referring to the person being welcomed or dative referring to the person doing the welcoming.

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|<hiero>ii-w</hiero>|read1=jjw
|<hiero>ii-w&y</hiero>|read2=jjwj
|<hiero>ii--i-D54-w&y</hiero>|read3=jjwj}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|egy|jj.tj}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Allen|337}}
* {{R:egy:Wb|1|38.1–38.4}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner|10}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Stative stem of {{affix|egy|jj|gloss1=to come|.tj|pos2=second-person singular stative ending}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Interjection===
{{egy-interj|head=<hiero>ii-ti</hiero>}}

# [[welcome]] {{gloss|greeting upon someone’s arrival}}

====Usage notes====
Syntactically this word functions as an adverbial (like other stative verb forms). It is usually followed by {{m|egy|m ḥtp||in peace}}.

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|<hiero>ii-i-D54-ti-i</hiero>|read1=jj.tj
|<hiero>ii-i-y:D54-ti-i</hiero>|read2=jj.tj}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|egy|jjwj}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Wb|1|38.5–38.6}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner|10}}
* {{R:egy:Allen|218}}
* {{R:egy:Hoch|116}}

==Egyptian==
{{egy-rom|jy,t}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|egy|jj||to come}}, thus literally ‘that which has come’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Speculatively, from {{inh|egy|afa-pro|*ʕal-}}; as with other attempts at reconstructing Proto-Afroasiatic, academic consensus is lacking. If so, perhaps compare {{cog|he|עָלָה|tr=ʕālā||to ascend, rise, go up}}, {{cog|ar|عَلِيَ||to be high, exalted}}, {{m|ar|عَلَى||to climb}}, {{cog|rif|aři||to climb, ascend}}, {{cog|tzm|ⴰⵍⵢ||to climb, go up}}

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{af|egy|jꜥḥ|t1=[[Iah]]/the moon|ḥtp|t2=to be content|.w|alt3=(.w)|pos3=masculine singular stative ending}}, thus literally ‘Iah/the moon is content’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|egy|/ˈjaʕħuw ˈħatpaw/|a=Old Egyptian}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

