==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{af|egy|jwj|alt1=jw|t1=comes|zp|t2=time, matter, misdeed}}, literally ‘(one’s) misdeed comes’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Phrase===
{{head|egy|phrase|head=<hiero>D54-w-z:p*zp-nDs</hiero>}}

# {{lb|egy|with following suffix pronoun|usually negated}} to be found [[responsible]] for [[fault]]s or [[misdeed]]s, to have [[find fault|fault found]] with one
#: {{coi|egy|<hiero>D35:D54-w-z:p*zp-nDs-A1</hiero>
|tr=nj '''jw zp'''.j
|no '''fault was found with''' me}}
#: {{coi|egy|<hiero>ii-w-z:p*zp-f</hiero>
|tr='''jjw zp'''.f
|he '''with whom fault was found'''}}

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|<hiero>ii-w-z:p*zp</hiero>|read1=jjw zp
|<hiero>D54-w-z:p*zp</hiero>|read2=jw zp}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Wb|1|44.23}}
* {{R:egy:Wb|3|435.9}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner|10–12}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{af|egy|jw|pos1=imperfective relative form of {{m|egy|jwj||to come}}|.f|t2=he, it|pw|t3=this is...}}, literally ‘it is that it comes’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Phrase===
{{head|egy|phrase|head=<hiero>D54-w-f:p-w</hiero>}}

# {{ng|formulaic statement made in the [[colophon]] or [[conclusion]] of a literary text}}; that’s how it goes, [[the end]] {{defdate|Middle Kingdom to Late Period}}
#* {{Q|egy||Kagemni|lines 2.8–2.9|quote=<hiero>aHa-a:n-r:a-<!--2.9-->kA-Z1-gm-m-n:A1-A1-r-m:r-niwt:t*Z1-TA-t:A1-!-D54-W-f-p-W</hiero>
|tr=ꜥḥꜥ.n rdj kꜣ-gm-n.j r jmj-r nwt ṯꜣt(j) '''jw.f pw'''
|t=Then Kagemni was made overseer of the city and vizier. '''That’s how it goes. / The end.'''}}

====Usage notes====
In literature of the Middle Kingdom this formula is often extended to {{m|egy|jw.f pw [[ḥꜣt]][[.f]] [[r]] [[pḥwj]][[.fj]]||that’s how it goes, its beginning to its end}}; in the New Kingdom, it is instead often extended to {{m|egy|jw.f pw [[m ḥtp]]||that’s how it’s successfully concluded|lit=it is that it comes in peace}}.

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|<hiero>E17-f:p-w</hiero>|read1=jw.f pw|date1=Late Period}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|egy|jw.s pw}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Wb|1|45.1–45.3}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner|12}}
* {{R:egy:Allen|376}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{af|egy|jw|pos1=imperfective relative form of {{m|egy|jwj||to come}}|.s|t2=she, it|pw|t3=this is...}}, literally ‘it is that it comes’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Phrase===
{{head|egy|phrase|head=<hiero>D54-w-s-p-w</hiero>}}

# {{lb|egy|Late Egyptian}} {{ng|formulaic statement made in the [[colophon]] or [[conclusion]] of a literary text}}; that’s how it goes, [[the end]]

====Usage notes====
This formula is often extended to {{m|egy|jw.s pw [[nfr]]||so it comes to a good conclusion}} or further to {{m|egy|jw.s pw [[nfr]] [[m ḥtp]]||so it successfully comes to a good conclusion}}.

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|<hiero>D54:W-s-p:W</hiero>|read1=jw.s pw}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|egy|jw.f pw}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Wb|1|45.4}}
* {{R:egy:Allen|376}}

===Etymology 1===
Speculatively, from {{inh|egy|afa-pro|*lib-||heart}}; as with other attempts at reconstructing Proto-Afroasiatic, academic consensus is lacking. If so, perhaps cognate with {{cog|sem-pro|*libb-}}<ref name=Loprieno>{{R:egy:Loprieno|31}}</ref> and {{cog|ber-pro|*ulβ}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-R|o=jib|m=jib|ml=ʔeb|l=ʔep
|onote=<ref name=Loprieno/>}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

