etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Dual form of {{m|egy|pw}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Determiner===
{{egy-det|m-d|proximal, later vocative|head=i-p-w&y}}

# {{lb|egy|Old Egyptian}} [[these]] [[two]]
# {{lb|egy|Middle Egyptian|archaizing}} [[O]] {{gloss|vocative reference}}

====Usage notes====
This demonstrative was originally a determiner but could later be used alone, like a pronoun. When used as a determiner it follows the noun it describes.

In Old Egyptian it would hypothetically form a contrastive pair with the demonstrative {{m|egy|*jpfj}}, in which {{m|egy||jpwj}} is [[proximal]]. However, in Old Egyptian texts both {{m|egy||jpwj}} and {{m|egy|*jpfj}} are only attested in written forms identical to those of the plural demonstratives {{m|egy|jpw}} and {{m|egy|jpf}} (and in one case the singular {{m|egy|pw}}), so that the separate existence of the dual forms is a matter of inference rather than clear attestation.

The term’s use in Middle Egyptian texts is an archaism. However, this is the only context in which it can be found spelled in full and clearly distinct from the plural {{m|egy|jpw}}.

====Inflection====
{{Egyptian demonstratives}}

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|i-p-w|read1=jpw
|p-w|read2=pw|note2=rare}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:TLA|jpwj|500484}}
* {{R:egy:Wb|1|69.8}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner|17}}
* {{R:egy:Allen|311}}
* {{R:egy:Edel|83 et seq.|182 et seq.}}
* {{R:egy:Plural|62–63|61}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Plural form of {{m|egy|pf}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Determiner===
{{egy-det|m-p|distal|head=i-p:f}}

# {{lb|egy|Old Egyptian}} [[those]]

====Usage notes====
This demonstrative was originally a determiner but could later be used alone, like a pronoun. When used as a determiner it follows or precedes the noun it describes.

In Old Egyptian it forms a contrastive pair with the demonstrative {{m|egy|jpn}}, in which {{m|egy||jpf}} is [[distal]].

By Middle Egyptian it is obsolete.

In Old Egyptian this form is also used for the dual. Traditionally this is interpreted as a summary writing of a special dual form {{m|egy|*jpfj}}. An alternative possible interpretation is that there simply was no distinction between the masculine dual and plural demonstrative determiners.

====Inflection====
{{Egyptian demonstratives}}

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|p:f|read1=pf|note1=uncommon}}

