etymologies.etymology_text:
===Etymology 1===

====Suffix====
{{egy-suffix|head=<hiero>i-i-t</hiero>}}

# {{ng|Forms the [[complementary infinitive]] of weak verbs.}}

=====Usage notes=====
Weak verbs can alternatively take the endings {{m|egy|-t}} or {{m|egy|-wt}} to form the complementary infinitive.

===Etymology 2===

====Suffix====
{{egy-suffix|head=<hiero>i-i-t</hiero>}}

# {{ng|Forms the [[terminative]] of third-weak verbs, more frequently when passive than when active.}}

=====Usage notes=====
Third-weak verbs can alternatively take the ending {{m|egy|-t}}, as they usually do when active.

===Etymology 1===
Possibly related to {{cog|sem-pro|*yad-||hand}}.

====Pronunciation====
