etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Perhaps a noun of instrument from the verb {{m|egy|ꜥnb||to close, to twine around}}, as proposed by Osing; however, the meaning of this verb is not entirely clear.<ref name=Dils>Dils, Peter (2021), “Papyrus Brooklyn 47.218.02” in [https://sae.saw-leipzig.de/de/dokumente/papyrus-brooklyn-4721802?version=16 ''Science in Ancient Egypt'']</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|m=ʕVˈnaːbVw|ml=ʕaˈnaːbə|l=ʕaˈnoːβ(ə)|V=1}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==
{{wikipedia|Ankh wedja seneb}}

===Etymology===
Traditionally considered to be a series of nouns {{compound|egy|ꜥnḫ|wḏꜣ|snb}}, literally meaning ‘life, prosperity, health (to him)’. More recently the phrase has instead been analyzed as a series of verbs, each with the unwritten stative ending {{m|egy|.w}}, thus literally meaning ‘(may he be) alive, sound, healthy’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Interjection===
{{egy-interj|head=<hiero>S34-U28-s</hiero>}}

# {{non-gloss|an honorific phrase used after the names of kings, queens, princes, etc., after the words of a king, ruler, or prince, after references to the royal household, and, more rarely, after the names of ordinary people.}}

====Derived terms====
{{col2|egy
|rdj ꜥnḫ wḏꜣ snb
|ḥr tp ꜥnḫ wḏꜣ snb
|m ꜥnḫ wḏꜣ snb}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Faulkner}}
* {{R:egy:Wb}}
* {{R:egy:Allen|221}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{compound|egy|ꜥnḫ|gloss1=to live|.w|alt2=(.w)|pos2=third-person masculine singular stative ending|ḏt|gloss3=forever}}, literally meaning ‘alive forever’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Interjection===
{{egy-interj|head=<hiero>anx-D&t&tA</hiero>}}

# {{non-gloss|an honorific phrase used after the [[nomen]] or [[praenomen]] of a (male) pharaoh.}}

====See also====
* {{l|egy|ꜥnḫ.tj ḏt}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Allen|221}}
* {{R:egy:Hoch|116}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{affix|egy|ꜥnḫ|gloss1=to live|.tj|pos2=third-person feminine singular stative ending}}, literally meaning ‘alive’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Interjection===
{{egy-interj|head=anx-ti}}

# {{non-gloss|an honorific phrase used after the names of queens and princesses.}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Allen|221}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{compound|egy|ꜥnḫ|gloss1=to live|.tj|pos2=third-person feminine singular stative ending|ḏt|gloss3=forever}}, literally meaning ‘alive forever’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Interjection===
{{egy-interj|head=anx-ti-i-D&t&tA}}

# {{non-gloss|an honorific phrase used after the [[nomen]] or [[praenomen]] of a (female) pharaoh.}}

====See also====
* {{l|egy|ꜥnḫ ḏt}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Hoch|116}}

===Etymology 1===
Sometimes proposed to be from a form such as {{inh|egy|afa-pro|*ʔar-ḳ-|t=to see, to understand}}. Compare {{cog|cus-pro|*ʔark’-|t=to see, to understand}}. 

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˈʕaːlaqʼ|m=ˈʕaːlaqʼ|ml=ˈʕaːləqʼ|l=ˈʕoːləqʼ}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Etymology 2===
From a form of the verb above.

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ʕaˈlaqʼ|m=ʕaˈlaqʼ|ml=ʕaˈlaqʼ|l=ʕaˈlaqʼ
|onote=&#x20;{{q|singular}}; {{IPA|egy|/ʕaˈlaːqʼaw/}} {{q|plural}}
|mnote=&#x20;{{q|singular}}; {{IPA|egy|/ʕaˈlaːqʼaw/}} {{q|plural}}
|mlnote=&#x20;{{q|singular}}; {{IPA|egy|/ʕaˈlaːqʼə/}} {{q|plural}}
|lnote=&#x20;{{q|singular}}; {{IPA|egy|/ʕaˈloːqʼ/}} {{q|plural}}}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
From {{af|egy|ꜥrq|t1=to tie on, to complete, to stop|-y}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ʕVlˈq’iw|m=ʕVlˈq’ij|ml=ʕalˈq’eʔ|l=ʕalˈq’eʔ|V=1}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

