==Egyptian==

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=piʀ|m=piʀ|ml=pə|l=pə}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Determiner===
{{egy-det|m-s|anaphoric|head=<hiero>pA</hiero>}}

# {{lb|egy|Old and Late Egyptian}} [[O]] {{gloss|vocative reference}}
# {{lb|egy|Middle Egyptian}} the [[aforementioned]], the [[said]]
# {{lb|egy|Late Egyptian}} {{ng|the definite article}}; [[the]]
# {{lb|egy|Late Egyptian|with following noun}} [[he]] [[of]], [[this]] [[of]], [[that]] [[of]]

====Usage notes====
This demonstrative was originally a determiner but could later be used alone, like a pronoun. When used as a determiner it precedes the noun it describes.

In Middle Egyptian, this pronoun was possibly somewhat colloquial; in Late Egyptian its force had weakened to that of a definite article.

====Inflection====
{{Egyptian demonstratives}}

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|<hiero>pA-A</hiero>|read1=pꜣ
|<hiero>G41-A</hiero>|read2=pꜣ}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|egx-dem|pꜣ}}
** {{desc|cop|ⲡ-}} {{q|Sahidic|Fayyumic|Akhmimic|Lycopolitan}}, {{l|cop|ⲡⲉ-}} {{q|Sahidic|Fayyumic|Lycopolitan}}, {{l|cop|ⲡⲓ-}} {{q|Bohairic|Fayyumic}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Allen|54–56}}
* {{R:egy:Junge|53}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner|87}}
* {{R:egy:Loprieno|68–70}}

{{cln|egy|articles}}

==Egyptian==

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Determiner===
{{egy-det|m-s|head=<hiero>pA-i-i</hiero>}}

# {{lb|egy|Late Egyptian|with attached suffix pronoun}} {{ng|forms [[possessive]]s}}; [[my]], [[our]], [[your]], [[his]], [[her]], [[its]], [[their]], {{ng|depending on which suffix pronoun is attached}}

====Usage notes====
This determiner modifies masculine singular nouns, but it does not specify that the possessor is masculine singular; the gender and number of the possessor are specified by the attached suffix pronoun.

====Inflection====
{{Egyptian demonstratives}}

For the possible suffix pronoun endings, see [[:Template:Egyptian personal pronouns]].

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|<hiero>pA-A-i-i</hiero>|read1=pꜣy
|<hiero>G41-A-i-i</hiero>|read2=pꜣy}}

