===Etymology===
{{compound|egy|pꜣ|nj|alt2=n(j)|pꜣ|mḫrw}}, literally ‘the one of the censer’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|egy|/pə nə pə məˈχiːɾ/|a=Late Egyptian}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Compare with {{cog|akk|𒉺𒀀𒄣|tr=pa-a-qu|ts=pāqu, piāqu|t=narrow}} and {{cog|ar|ف و ق|lit=the small notch of the clavicle, the top of the shoulders, the thin dimensions of the coronal plane looking down from above the torso}}, verb forms VII and VIII showing its connection to shortness, to become thin, emaciated, to wear out, and to die of coughing or shortness of breath, gasping.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˈpiʀqʼit|m=ˈpiʀqʼiʔ|ml=ˈpiːqʼa|l=ˈpiːqʼə}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

