etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Determiner===
{{egy-det|m-s|distal|head=p:f}}

# [[that]]

====Usage notes====
This demonstrative was originally a determiner but could later be used alone, like a pronoun. When used as a determiner it follows or precedes the noun it describes.

It forms a contrastive pair with the demonstrative {{m|egy|pn}}, in which {{m-self|egy||pf}} is [[distal]].

In Old Egyptian this form was occasionally used in place of the plural {{m|egy|jpf}}. Whether this should be interpreted as a mere summarily written variant of {{m|egy|jpf}} or as a genuine use of the singular for the plural is unclear.

====Inflection====
{{Egyptian demonstratives}}

====Alternative forms====
{{egy-hieroforms
|p:f-A-N31|read1=pfꜣ|date1=since the Middle Kingdom}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Allen|54–55}}
* {{R:egy:Edel|83 et seq.|182 et seq.}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner}}

==Egyptian==

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Determiner===
{{egy-det|m-s|proximal|head=p:n}}

# [[this]], [[that]]

====Usage notes====
This demonstrative was originally a determiner but could later be used alone, like a pronoun. When used as a determiner it follows the noun it describes.

It forms a contrastive pair with the demonstrative {{m|egy|pf}}, in which {{m|egy||pn}} is [[proximal]].

In Old Egyptian this form was occasionally used in place of the plural {{m|egy|jpn}}. Whether this should be interpreted as a mere summarily written variant of {{m|egy|jpn}} or as a genuine use of the singular for the plural is unclear.

====Inflection====
{{Egyptian demonstratives}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Allen|54–55}}
* {{R:egy:Edel|83 et seq.|182 et seq.}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner}}

