==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{af|egy|pr|t1=house|ḥḏ|t2=silver}} in a direct genitive construction, thus ‘house of silver’. However, this may be a reanalysis, and the name may have originally been intended as {{af|egy|pr|t1=house|ḥḏ|t2=white}}, thus ‘white house’, in contrast to the treasury of Lower Egypt, {{m|egy|pr-dšr|lit=the red house}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˌpaɾuwˈħicʼ|m=ˌpaɾuwˈħitʼ|ml=pəɾəˈħetʼ|l=pəɾəˈħetʼ}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|egy|prj||to emerge}}; the different Coptic descendants show that the derivation is not the same as that of {{m|egy||prt|season of Emergence}}. Compare {{cog|he|פְּרִי|tr=pri||fruit}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-R|o=puˈɾut|m=puˈɾuʔ|ml=pəˈɾuʔ|l=pəˈɾøʔ
|onote=<ref name=Loprieno>{{R:egy:Loprieno}}</ref>}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{af|egy|prt|pos1=infinitive of {{m|egy|prj||to emerge}}|ḫrw|t2=voice}}, thus ‘emergence of the voice’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˌpiɾitχaˈɾaw|m=ˌpiɾiʔχaˈɾaw|ml=ˌpəɾəχəˈɾaw|l=ˌpəɾəχəˈɾaw}}
