etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
An origin in a form such as {{inh|egy|afa-pro|*maʔ-}} has been suggested, but as with other attempts at reconstructing Proto-Afroasiatic, academic consensus is lacking; compare {{cog|sem-pro|*māy-}}. The word is a frozen plural, with an original root {{m|egy||*m}} or {{m|egy||*mj}}, the latter of which is supported by the phonetic use of the hieroglyph to write {{m|egy|nmjw||dwarf}}. Compare also {{m|egy|rmj}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=maw|m=maw|ml=maw|l=maw|ref=<ref>{{R:egy:Loprieno|12, 44}}</ref>}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Etymology 1===
Likely a [[babble word]] in origin, like many of its Afroasiatic parallels.<ref>{{R:egy:EDE|3|193–195}}</ref> Militarev and Stolbova derive it from a supposed {{inh|egy|afa-pro|-}} form instead, but also note it may be a nursery word.<ref>{{cite-web|author=Militarev, Alexander and Stolbova, Olga|year=2007|url=http://starling.rinet.ru/cgi-bin/response.cgi?single=1&basename=%2fdata%2fsemham%2fafaset&text_number=2449&root=config|title=*ˀVma/*ma(y)|work=Afroasiatic etymology database at StarLing}}</ref> If not, perhaps cognate with {{cog|sem-pro|*ʔimm-}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˈmiʔwat|m=ˈmiʔwaʔ|ml=ˈmeʔwə|l=ˈmeʔw
|onote=<ref>{{R:egy:Loprieno|245|passage=*/ˈmeʔwat/}}</ref>}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|egy|afa-pro|*mawVt-||to die, to kill}}. Cognate with {{cog|sem-pro|*mawut-}}, {{cog|tzm|ⵎⵎⵜ}} and {{cog|ha|mutù}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˈmaːwat|m=ˈmaːjaʔ|ml=ˈmaːʔə|l=ˈmoːʔ}}
