==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
From {{af|egy|mn <t:established, enduring>|ḫpr <t:manifestation, form>|rꜥ <t:Ra>}}, thus literally ‘the Established One of the Manifestation of Ra’. {{egy-ht}}

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
From {{af|egy|m-|pos1=noun-forming prefix|wnḫ|t2=to clothe|-t|pos3=feminine suffix}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|q=noun and proper noun|o=mawˈnaːχit|m=mawˈnaːχiʔ|ml=məˈnaːχa|l=məˈnoːχə}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|egy|ail}}
Perhaps from {{inh|egy|afa-pro|-}}. Possible Berber cognates include the forms represented by {{cog|kab|umran|u-mr-an|sorrows}}, {{m|kab|amur|a-mur|colic, stomachache}}, and {{m|kab|amrir|a-mrir|embarrassment, great difficulty}}. Possible Cushitic cognates include {{cog|om|marar|t=to be sick}}, {{cog|bsw|marni|t=to be sad}}, and {{cog|sid|marars|marar-s|to be sick}}. A proposed Omotic cognate is {{cog|jnj|mero|mer-o|illness}}. Also compare the root {{cog|ar|م ر ض|t=related to ailment|tr=m-r-ḍ}}.

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|egy|canal}}
Possibly from a {{inh|egy|afa-pro|*m-r|t=river, channel}}. Compare South {{cog|omv}} *''mir-'' (“river”), with reflexes including {{cog|aiw|mɨri|t=river, stream}} and {{cog|dim|mɪ́rɛ|t=river}}. A possible Semitic cognate is {{cog|xsa|𐩣𐩧|t=part of an irrigation system|tr=mr}}. Possible Cushitic cognates include Borana {{cog|om|mērī|t=watering trough}}, {{cog|tsb|mīre|t=pond}}, and possible Chadic cognates include {{cog|fli|mirə̂|t=river}}, {{cog|mje|mìrà|t=oxbow lake, [[marigot]]}}.

===Etymology 5===
{{etymid|egy|bull}}
Perhaps from {{inh|egy|afa-pro|-}}. Cognate with {{cog|sem-pro|*mir(Vʔ)-|t=bull}}: compare {{cog|akk|𒈪𒅕𒋾|t=young cow|tr=mīrtu}}, {{m|akk|𒄞𒀖|t=young bull|tr=mīru}}, {{cog|he|מְרִיא|t=fatted steer|tr=mərīʾ}}. Possible Cushitic cognates include {{cog|hdy|mōr-â|t=bull}}, {{cog|mhd|ki-mole}}, {{m|mhd|ki-more|t=ox, bull}}, possible Omotic cognates include {{cog|wal|mārā|t=young bull}}, {{cog|jnj|omoru|t=bull}}, and possible Chadic cognates include {{cog|maf|maray|t=sacrificial bull}}, {{cog|mif|maray|t=fattened bull}}, {{cog|maf|mari|t=bull}}.

