* {{R:egy:Allen|56}}
* {{R:egy:Faulkner}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
{{compound|egy|nj|t1=not|zpj|alt2=zp|t2=to happen}} in the [[perfective]].

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Phrase===
{{head|egy|phrase|head=<hiero>D35-z:p*zp</hiero>}}

# {{lb|egy|with a following verb in the subjunctive}} [[never]] (has it happened that…); {{ng|used as a stronger version of the negation of a perfective with {{m|egy|nj}}.}}
#* {{Q|egy||ShS.|lines 153–154|quote=<hiero><!--153-->xpr-r-i-s-E9-w-d-D54-k\-t-w-r-st-t:pr-t:n-!-D35:z-p:zp-<!--154-->U2:ir-A-k\-N18:N23*Z1-p:n-xpr-r-m-n:U19-nw-W-i-i-mw</hiero>
|tr=ḫpr js jwd.k tw r st pn '''nj zp''' mꜣ.k jw pn ḫpr(.w) m nwy
|t=When your parting from this place comes to pass, you '''will never again''' see this island, which will have turned into water.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|egy|nj zp jwt ḫt nb jm}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Allen|270}}

==Egyptian==

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

===Suffix===
{{egy-suffix|head=<hiero>nw</hiero>}}

# {{ng|Added to the roots of [[cardinal number]]s to form the [[ordinal number]]s [[second]] through [[ninth]].}}

====Inflection====
{{egy-decl-adj|nw|hiero1=<hiero>nw</hiero>|nwt|hiero2=<hiero>nw:t</hiero>|-|-|-|-|nonotes=1}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Allen|103}}

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
{{egy-IPA-E}}

====Determiner====
{{egy-det|head=<hiero>nb</hiero>}}

# [[all]], [[every]]
# [[every other]]
# all [[sort]]s of, all [[kind]]s of
# {{lb|egy|especially in negated clauses}} [[any]]

=====Inflection=====
{{egy-decl-adj|nb}}

In the Pyramid Texts of Unas, among certain other Old Egyptian texts, {{m|egy||nb}} is usually not inflected by gender and number but invariably appears as {{m|egy||nb}}. Even within these texts, however, inflected forms sporadically appear.<ref>Allen, James P. (2017) ''A Grammar of the Ancient Egyptian Pyramid Texts, Volume 1: Unis'', page 55</ref>

In Late Egyptian, as all forms collapsed together with the masculine singular, the usual writing of the word came to follow the old feminine singular, {{m|egy|<hiero>nb:t</hiero>|tr={{l|egy|nbt}}}}.

=====Alternative forms=====
{{egy-hieroforms
|<hiero>n:nb</hiero>|read1=nb|date1=Old and Middle Kingdoms|note1=rare
|<hiero>nb:t</hiero>|read2=nbt|date2=Late Egyptian
|<hiero>nbw</hiero>|read3=nbw|date3=Greco-Roman Period
|<hiero>E1</hiero>|read4=nb|date4=Greco-Roman Period
|<hiero>N-b</hiero>|read5=nb|date5=Greco-Roman Period}}

