===Etymology===
{{af|egy|nqꜥ|t1=to scratch|-wt}}. Sycamore figs were scraped or gashed in order to make them ripen more quickly; otherwise, they would be full of insects and inedible by the time they ripened.<ref>Galil, J. (1967) “An Ancient Technique for Ripening Sycomore Fruit in East Mediterranean Countries”</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|egy|/nəˈqʼoːʔ/|a=Late Egyptian}}
* {{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==
{{wikipedia|Neith}}

