etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Possibly from a form such as {{inh|egy|afa-pro|*xanam}}; compare {{cog|ar|غَنَم||sheep and goats}}.<ref>{{R:egy:Loprieno|35}}</ref> Also compare {{cog|rif|amyan|t=goat}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=çVˈnaːmVw|m=çVˈnaːmVw|ml=çəˈnaːmə|l=çəˈnoːm|V=1}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==
{{wikipedia|Khufu}}

===Etymology===
{{af|egy|ẖnmw|t1=[[Khnum]]|ḫwj|alt2=ḫw|t2=shall protect|pos2=subjunctive mood of {{m|egy|ḫwj||to protect}}|.f|t3=he|wj|t4=me}}, thus literally ’[[Khnum]], he shall protect me’.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-E}}

ẖr.references:
* {{R:egy:Wb|3|386.1–388.15}}
* {{R:egy:Allen|89}}
