etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
Compare {{cog|sem-pro|*šamaʕ-||to hear, to listen}}. Unrelated to {{ncog|ine-pro|*sh₂em-|t=to sing}} ({{ncog|sa|सामन्}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˈsaːcʼam|m=ˈsaːtʼam|ml=ˈsaːtʼəm|l=ˈsoːtʼəm
|onote=&#x20;{{q|infinitive}}; {{IPA|egy|/saˈcʼimna/}} {{q|perfect}}, {{IPA|egy|/sacʼˈma/}} {{q|subjunctive}}, {{IPA|egy|/ˈsaːcʼim/}} {{q|active participle}}, {{IPA|egy|/ˈsacʼmiw/}} {{q|passive participle}}<ref name=Loprieno>{{R:egy:Loprieno|53}}</ref>
|mnote=&#x20;{{q|infinitive}}
|mlnote=&#x20;{{q|infinitive}}
|lnote=&#x20;{{q|infinitive}}}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==

===Etymology===
From {{af|egy|s-|pos1=causative prefix|ḏd|t2=to say}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-IPA-R|o=ˈsicʼtʼit|m=ˈsit͡ʃʔʼiʔ|ml=ˈset͡ʃʼa|l=ˈset͡ʃʼə
|onote=&#x20;{{q|infinitive}}<ref>{{R:egy:Loprieno|49, 53}}</ref>
|mnote=&#x20;{{q|infinitive}}; for the change {{IPAfont|/tʼ/}} → {{IPAfont|/ʔ/}} see {{m|egy|ḏd}}
|mlnote=&#x20;{{q|infinitive}}
|lnote=&#x20;{{q|infinitive}}}}
{{egy-IPA-E}}

==Egyptian==
{{wikipedia|Shasu}}

===Etymology===
