|}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Gardiner|476}}
* {{R:egy:Calligraphy}}
* {{R:egy:Betrò}}
* {{R:egy:Peust|48}}

==Egyptian==

===Glyph origin===
Representing an Egyptian [[cobra]] ({{taxlink|Naja haje|species}}) in a position of rest. {{egy-hiero-color|yellow}} The phonogrammatic value derives by the [[rebus principle]] from its use as a logogram for {{m|egy|ḏt||cobra}}.

===Symbol===
{{head|egy|symbol|head=<hiero>D</hiero>|tr=ḏ}}

# {{ng|[[uniliteral|Uniliteral]] [[phonogram]] for {{m|egy||ḏ}}; since Middle Egyptian sometimes used for {{m|egy||d}}, as the sounds had merged in some phonetic environments.}}
# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|ḏt||cobra}}.}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Gardiner|476}}
* {{R:egy:Betrò}}
* {{R:egy:Peust|48}}

==Egyptian==

===Glyph origin===
<div>Representing two [[cobra]]s, a reduplication of <hiero>D</hiero> ({{m|egy|𓆓}}), the phonogram for {{m|egy||ḏ}}.</div>

===Symbol===
{{head|egy|symbol|head=<hiero>DD</hiero>|tr=ḏḏ}}

# {{ng|[[biliteral|Biliteral]] [[phonogram]] for {{m|egy||ḏḏ}}.}}

