etymologies.etymology_text:
==Egyptian==

===Glyph origin===
<div>Representing a papyrus roll, tied and sealed, showing the ends of the strings; a later development of <hiero>Y2</hiero> ({{m|egy|𓏝}}). Sometimes oriented vertically, <hiero>Y1V</hiero> ({{m|egy|𓏜}}).</div>

===Symbol===
{{head|egy|symbol|head=<hiero>Y1</hiero>|tr=mḏꜣt}}

# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|mḏꜣt||book}}.}} {{defdate|since the 12th Dynasty}}
# {{ng|[[phonogram|Phonogram]] for {{m|egy||mḏꜣt}}.}} {{defdate|since the 12th Dynasty}}
# {{ng|[[determinative|Determinative]] for writing and written things, as in {{m|egy|zẖꜣ||to write}}, {{m|egy|mdwt||words}}.}} {{defdate|since the 12th Dynasty}}
# {{ng|[[determinative|Determinative]] for abstract notions, as in {{m|egy|mꜣꜥt||truth}}, {{m|egy|rḫ||to know}}.}} {{defdate|since the 12th Dynasty}}
# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|dmḏ||total}} (in mathematical books and accounts).}} {{defdate|since the 12th Dynasty}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Gardiner|533}}
* {{R:egy:Calligraphy|51}}

==Egyptian==

===Glyph origin===
<div>Representing a papyrus roll, tied and sealed. Since the Middle Kingdom, the roll with tied ends <hiero>Y1</hiero> ({{m|egy|𓏛}}) has been used in place of this glyph.</div>

===Symbol===
{{head|egy|symbol|head=<hiero>Y2</hiero>|tr=mḏꜣt}}

# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|mḏꜣt||book}}.}} {{defdate|Old Kingdom}}
# {{ng|[[phonogram|Phonogram]] for {{m|egy||mḏꜣt}}.}} {{defdate|Old Kingdom}}
# {{ng|[[determinative|Determinative]] for writing and written things, as in {{m|egy|zẖꜣ||to write}}, {{m|egy|mdwt||words}}.}} {{defdate|Old Kingdom}}
# {{ng|[[determinative|Determinative]] for abstract notions, as in {{m|egy|mꜣꜥt||truth}}, {{m|egy|rḫ||to know}}.}} {{defdate|Old Kingdom}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Gardiner|533}}
* {{R:egy:Calligraphy|51}}

==Egyptian==

===Glyph origin===
<div>Showing two strokes, often diagonal <hiero>y</hiero> but sometimes vertical <hiero>Z1-Z1</hiero>, to represent duality. Compare the Chinese characters {{m|mul|二|sc=Hani}} and {{m|mul|⺀|sc=Hani}}. {{egy-hiero-color|black}} The phonogrammatic value of {{m|egy||j}} is derived from its use as the dual ending, {{m|egy|-j}}.</div>

===Symbol===
{{head|egy|symbol|head=<hiero>y</hiero>|tr=j}}

# {{ng|[[uniliteral|Uniliteral]] [[phonogram]] for {{m|egy||j}}.}} {{defdate|since the Middle Kingdom}}
# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|-j|pos=dual ending}}, originally replacing (for superstitious reasons) the device of writing the determinative twice in certain contexts.}} {{defdate|since the Pyramid Texts}}
# {{ng|Written in place of two difficult-to-draw signs.}} {{defdate|mostly since the 19th Dynasty}}

====Usage notes====
<div>Some [[Appendix:Egyptian transliteration schemes|transliteration schemes]] treat this glyph as a phonogrammatic variant of <hiero>i</hiero> ({{m|egy||j}}), while others treat it as a variant of <hiero>i-i</hiero> ({{m|egy||y}}), and some treat all three as equivalent.</div>

===References===
* {{R:egy:Gardiner|536–537}}
* {{R:egy:Peust|48}}

==Egyptian==
{{multiple images|perrow = 2|total_width=180
| image1 = Abydos-Bold-hieroglyph-Aa1.png  |width1=90|height1=90
| image2 = Hieroglyph Aa1 color Sarenput II.jpg  |width2=90|height2=90
| image3 = Hieratic Aa1 5D.png  |width3=90|height3=90
| image4 = Hieratic Aa1 19D.png  |width4=90|height4=90
| footer = Top left: hieroglyph Aa1 (stylized); right: in color, 12th Dynasty. <br/>Bottom left: hieratic, 5th Dynasty; right: 19th D. (similar forms common 11th-20th).
}}

===Glyph origin===
Disputed; a sieve and a human placenta have been proposed as possibilities. In the Archaic Period it was generally crosshatched horizontally and vertically, and this form sometimes appeared through the Old Kingdom. For most of Egyptian history through the New Kingdom a form with only horizontal striations was used. A form with diagonal striations instead was rare before the Libyan Period. {{egy-hiero-color|green}} In some representations that lack striations, only its color differentiates it from other circular glyphs.

===Symbol===
{{head|egy|symbol|head=<hiero>x</hiero>|tr=ḫ}}

# {{ng|[[uniliteral|Uniliteral]] [[phonogram]] for {{m|egy||ḫ}}.}}
# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|ḫ||placenta<sup>?</sup>, child; to be a child}}.}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Gardiner|539}}
* {{R:egy:Calligraphy|12}}
* {{R:egy:Peust|48}}
* {{R:egy:Wb|3|217}}

==Egyptian==

===Glyph origin===
Representing perhaps a part of the steering gear of ships.

===Symbol===
{{head|egy|symbol|head=<hiero>Aa5</hiero>|tr=ḥpt}}

# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|ḥjpt||course}}.}}
# {{ng|[[biliteral|Biliteral]] [[phonogram]] for {{m|egy||ḥp}}, as in {{m|egy|ḥp||Apis}}, {{m|egy|ḥpy||Hapy}}, {{m|egy|ḥpt||steering oar}}.}}

